package andromeda:data-transform@0.1.0;

/// Data-transform plugin category — **non-UI**. Transforms Arrow record
/// batches in-process; no DOM emission imports.
///
/// **Accessibility:** not applicable at this boundary. The data-transform
/// category does not return user-visible UI; output is binary Arrow IPC
/// consumed by host curation primitives or downstream plugin categories.
/// A11y obligations attach to UI-emitting categories only (custom-dashboard).
///
/// **Security posture:** input + output byte sequences are bounded 8 MB
/// at the host boundary; plugin-returned bytes are NEVER logged verbatim
/// (per security plan §Logging Vector 4 + obs-plan §11 Project-specific
/// row 3). Plugins receive zero host imports beyond what their WIT
/// declares — capability-scoped sandboxing per arch §Design Philosophy.
world data-transform {
    /// Plugin's transform entry point. Called by the host for each batch
    /// of OTLP-ingested data needing transformation. `input` is Arrow IPC
    /// bytes (≤8 MB enforced at host); `output` on success is transformed
    /// Arrow IPC bytes (≤8 MB enforced before re-emit on Tauri Channel);
    /// `error` on failure is a sanitized one-liner (no full stack traces).
    export transform: func(input: list<u8>) -> result<list<u8>, string>;
}
